        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 13 at 1:23AM PST until November 15 at 10:00AM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 5 to 7 feet with sets to 8 to 9\nfeet at west facing beaches. High rip current risk.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...From 4 PM today to 10 AM PST Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Dangerous swimming and surfing conditions and\nlocalized beach erosion and overflow.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Tides will be falling during this time, but\nadjusted high tides will be near 7 feet which could combine with\nthe high surf to produce localized beach erosion and overflow\ninto parking lots and boardwalks. Surf begins to wane Sunday\nafternoon but may remain elevated for west-facing beaches into\nMonday.",
        "instruction": "Inexperienced swimmers should remain out of the water due to\ndangerous surf conditions.",
